IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fca-nouns`
IMPORT `fca-definitions`
IMPORT `fca-s3-application`
IMPORT `fca-s2-adjustment`
IMPORT `fca-court`

-- Tests for the court's powers and duties as regulative rules (fca-court.l4).
--
-- What can and cannot be asserted on this main build.  The outcome of a DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS in an #ASSERT, so each
-- rule's GUARD (the decision function that switches it on) is ASSERTED, and the rule itself is RUN with #TRACE.  The outcome expected
-- from the text is written above each #TRACE; the printed outcome is recorded in NOTES.md (finding on traces).  check.sh does not see a
-- trace outcome (a trace prints no assertion line), so these outcomes are read by eye, not counted.
-- The Act states no deadline for any of these, so no event is timed to a deadline; events are at time 1 after the start at time 0.

§ `Fixtures`

`an ordinary frustrated contract` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a frustrated contract of insurance` MEANS
    `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, JUST (Date 1 6 2020), Date 1 1 2000, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` MEANS
    `Sum facts` OF 1000, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`expenses of 300 with nothing added` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF TRUE, 300, 0, 0
`no expenses incurred` MEANS
    `Expenses facts` OF FALSE, 0, 0, 0
`insurance money paid, the court is considering recovery, no duty to insure` MEANS
    `Insurance facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`insurance money paid, the court is considering recovery, an express term to insure` MEANS
    `Insurance facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` MEANS
    `Obligor facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` MEANS
    `Contract provision facts` OF TRUE, FALSE
`a contract with no such provision` MEANS
    `Contract provision facts` OF FALSE, FALSE
`a wholly performed part that the court finds severable` MEANS
    `Severable part facts` OF JUST TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`a part not performed that the court finds severable` MEANS
    `Severable part facts` OF JUST TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

§ `s 2(3) -- the permission to allow the party to retain or recover`

-- guards
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the court may allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `no expenses incurred` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- expected: the court allows it at time 1 -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 2(3) the court's permission to allow the party to retain or recover` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` AT 1
-- expected: the court never uses the permission -> the permission stays open (an unused MAY is not a breach)
#TRACE `s 2(3) the court's permission to allow the party to retain or recover` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `give effect to the provision of the contract` AT 1
-- expected: no expenses -> no permission arises -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 2(3) the court's permission to allow the party to retain or recover` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a sum of 1000 paid under the contract before the discharge` `no expenses incurred` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `allow the party to retain or recover the whole or part of the sums` AT 1

§ `s 2(5) -- the permission to include overheads and personal work`

#ASSERT `s 2(5) the court may include a reasonable sum for overhead expenses and for work performed personally` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the court may include a reasonable sum for overhead expenses and for work performed personally` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no expenses incurred` EQUALS NOTHING
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 2(5) the court's permission to include overhead expenses and personal work` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `expenses of 300 with nothing added` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `include a reasonable sum for overhead expenses and for work performed personally` AT 1
-- expected: no expenses incurred -> the guard is NOTHING, not JUST TRUE, so the permission is not switched on -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 2(5) the court's permission to include overhead expenses and personal work` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `no expenses incurred` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `include a reasonable sum for overhead expenses and for work performed personally` AT 1

§ `s 2(7) -- the permission to treat the benefit as obtained by the person who assumed the obligations`

#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(7) the court may treat the benefit conferred on another person as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 2(7) the court's permission to treat the benefit as obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `treat the benefit as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` AT 1
-- expected: the court does not consider it just -> no permission -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 2(7) the court's permission to treat the benefit as obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a person who assumed obligations for a benefit conferred on a stranger` (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `treat the benefit as a benefit obtained by the person who assumed the obligations` AT 1

§ `s 2(6) -- the prohibition on taking the insurance sums into account`

#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court shall not take the insurance sums into account` `insurance money paid, the court is considering recovery, no duty to insure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(6) the court shall not take the insurance sums into account` `insurance money paid, the court is considering recovery, an express term to insure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- expected: the court takes the insurance sums into account -> the prohibition is broken (BREACH)
#TRACE `s 2(6) the court's prohibition on taking the insurance sums into account` `insurance money paid, the court is considering recovery, no duty to insure` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `take the insurance sums into account` AT 1
-- expected: the court does something else -> the prohibition stands (no deadline is stated, so it does not complete)
#TRACE `s 2(6) the court's prohibition on taking the insurance sums into account` `insurance money paid, the court is considering recovery, no duty to insure` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `give effect to the provision of the contract` AT 1
-- expected: the "unless" is met (an express term to insure): nothing is prohibited, so taking them into account is no breach -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 2(6) the court's prohibition on taking the insurance sums into account` `insurance money paid, the court is considering recovery, an express term to insure` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `take the insurance sums into account` AT 1

§ `s 3(3) -- the duty to give effect to the contract's own provision`

#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with no such provision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(3) the court is to give effect to the provision of the contract` `a frustrated contract of insurance` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- expected: the court gives effect to the provision -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 3(3) the court's duty to give effect to the provision of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `give effect to the provision of the contract` AT 1
-- expected: the court does nothing relevant -> the duty stays open (no deadline, so no breach)
#TRACE `s 3(3) the court's duty to give effect to the provision of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with a provision for the event of frustration` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `take the insurance sums into account` AT 1
-- expected: no such provision -> no duty arises -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 3(3) the court's duty to give effect to the provision of the contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a contract with no such provision` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `give effect to the provision of the contract` AT 1

§ `s 3(4) -- the duty to treat a severed part as a separate contract`

#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a wholly performed part that the court finds severable` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(4) the court is to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part not performed that the court finds severable` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 3(4) the court's duty to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a wholly performed part that the court finds severable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` AT 1
-- expected: the part was not performed -> no duty -> FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 3(4) the court's duty to treat the part of the contract as a separate contract` `an ordinary frustrated contract` `a part not performed that the court finds severable` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `treat the part of the contract as a separate contract that has not been frustrated` AT 1

-- assertions written: 13; satisfied: 13 (check.sh prints the count); traces: 15, run and read by eye
